   This is an OSK port of the netpbm (aka pbmplus) toolkit.  This is a pretty big package and contains some 170 standaloneprograms.  They can be used to make conversions between various graphicsformats.  They are compiled for a plain 68000.  Please note that someprograms (like ppmforge or pgmcrater) may be faster by a factor of 20-50if the whole package is recompiled to use the FPU coprocessor.  Because the whole package is large, I have split it into three parts:netpbm_cmds.lzh, netpbm_docs.lzh and netpbm_src.lzh  Documentation is available in PostScript, TeX and troff formats.  Andrzej Kotanski(kotanski@desy.de)                               Hamburg, March 27, 1998